<Layout title="About Us — Wild Family" description="Learn about Wild Family — a blog about family camping, hiking, and nature adventures, written for real families.">
  <section class="page-content container">
    <h1>About Wild Family</h1>
    <p>
      Wild Family started with a simple frustration: every "family camping guide" we found assumed you had a van, a thousand dollars of gear, and children who never complain. We have none of those things.
    </p>
    <p>
      So we started writing the guides we actually needed — the honest, practical kind. What do you really need for a first camping trip? How far can a toddler actually walk? What keeps kids entertained outside without a single screen?
    </p>
    <h2>What We Believe</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Nature doesn't need to be a big production. A backyard, a park bench, or a small trail is enough.</li>
      <li>Practical beats perfect. Checklists and simple plans beat Instagram-worthy setups.</li>
      <li>Kids remember mud, stories, and s'mores — not gear. Keep it simple and go.</li>
      <li>Every family deserves real outdoor time, whatever their budget.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What We Write</h2>
    <p>
      Camping checklists that work, hiking trails suited to little legs, screen-free activities that actually entertain, and the honest truth about what goes wrong — plus how to laugh about it later.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you're a family that wants more trees and fewer screens, you're in the right place.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/contact/">Get in touch →</a></p>
  </section>
</Layout>